WEBVTT

00:04.500 --> 00:16.500
An AI assistant on a plant floor was told to update
one work order — 4802. It did the job perfectly.
On the wrong work order.

00:17.500 --> 00:30.500
HAIEC doesn't take the agent's word for it — it compares
what the agent was told to touch against what the record
shows it actually touched. The target came back broader.

00:31.500 --> 00:45.000
So what does a human do? Walk with me.
Detect. Investigate. Authorize.

00:45.000 --> 00:62.000
Watch — I can pause the dispatcher right from the browser.
But look how honest the screen is: it's a rehearsal.
It's not touching real equipment.

00:63.000 --> 00:78.500
Everything we couldn't prove stays on screen,
marked not assessed. Unknown doesn't get
rounded up to "fine."

00:79.500 --> 00:90.500
Every finding links to a public receipt — anyone can check
the integrity of this exact evaluation. It's labeled
synthetic, because it is.

00:91.500 --> 01:07.000
Nine AI systems. Forty-five evaluations. Nine times the
target drifted — caught. Every single one still says
review. Here's what the evidence proves — and where it stops.

01:08.500 --> 01:16.500
That's HAIEC. Not a score. Not a guess. Verified facts,
explicit unknowns — and a human who finally knows
what they're looking at.
